{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-confinement-level-unique-local-constancy","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:confinement-level-unique-local-constancy","kind":"remark","title":"Local constancy of the confinement level in $q$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-confinement-level-unique"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-confinement-level-unique","tags":["uniqueness","confinement","filtration","shadow-price"],"text":"confinement-level-unique-local-constancy.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:confinement-level-unique-local-constancy\"></a><p>There is local uniqueness in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>. By the continuity of shadow prices on the generic locus, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell(K, q')</code> is locally constant on a neighborhood of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>, except at the boundary variety where some <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E(\\lambda, q) = 0</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/confinement-level-unique-local-constancy.md","heading":"Remark","number":"9.6.5"}
